# Study and participant IDs

Use these names on the admin sitting profile. They show up in exports and camera files (`table-{participant}-sitting{n}-{take}.webm`).

## Study ID = collection day

Format: `hti-YYYYMMDD`

- One ID per calendar day of data collection
- Example: `hti-20260902`

Do not put the participant number or sitting number in the study ID.

## Participant ID = person, not sitting

Format: `P##` (letter P + two digits, no spaces, no extra hyphens)

- Example: `P01`, `P02`, `P03`
- Reuse the same `P##` for that person’s sitting 1, 2, and 3
- Sitting stays in the Sitting dropdown only

## Allowed characters

Letters, numbers, `.`, `_`, `-` only. No spaces, slashes, or `..`.

```text
# Good
Study ID: hti-20260902
Participant ID: P01
Sitting: 2
Camera file: table-P01-sitting2-1.webm

# Bad
Study ID: pilot-01          (no date, collides across days)
Participant ID: P-001       (extra hyphen, sitting is not in this field)
Participant ID: owl / 3     (unsafe for filenames)
```
